Chapter 4: Architecture and System Design

4.1 AI Hierarchy: Architect, Foreman, Mason

· Architect (Strategic AI): An LLM‑based strategic planner with SPIN‑verified LTL output. It decomposes natural‑language goals into a sequence of partial target graphs \mathcal{G}_k^*, each guaranteed safe.
· Foreman (Orchestration AI): Executes the robust CBBA assignment and cluster‑level SCP trajectory generation every 60 s, maintains a digital twin for belief updates, and oversees the hierarchical MCTS planner. Resides on the Nucleus module.
· Mason (Edge Autonomy): Each tile runs a lightweight policy network distilled from the Foreman's GNN‑guided MCTS. It performs local sensor fusion, 6‑DOF EM dipole control with PCM thermal management, thruster allocation, and local CBF‑QP execution at 10 Hz. Communication loss triggers safe‑hold mode.

